Negative control for the scenario page's remount key (P1-R2).

Keys the page on `route.fullPath` again, so a criteria write into the QUERY
string tears the whole page down and re-boots the composable from scratch —
the defect the operator called "a big nono". `history.replaceState` (what
`useCriteriaUrlSync` writes through today) is invisible to vue-router, which
is why this hazard is silent: the covering spec must drive the write through
the ROUTER so the key is actually exercised.

Apply from the repo root: `git apply <this file>`; revert with `git apply -R`.

Reds: tests/e2e/criteria-clear-remount.spec.ts — "@P1-R2 a criteria change
carried by the ROUTER remounts nothing either" (measured 2026-08-10: 1 failed,
4 passed with the mutant applied). The sibling filter-write case stays green
under it on purpose: that write goes through `history.replaceState`, which
vue-router never observes, so only the router-carried case exercises the key.

--- a/playgrounds/labs-nuxt/app/pages/scenarios/[key]/[...scopeSuffix].vue
+++ b/playgrounds/labs-nuxt/app/pages/scenarios/[key]/[...scopeSuffix].vue
@@ -49,7 +49,7 @@
   // `/for/:type/:id`) are what the port is built from, so they must remount and
   // rebuild it — while the criteria, which task 58 persists into the QUERY
   // string, must not. A `fullPath` key ties a teardown to every filter write.
-  key: route => route.path,
+  key: route => route.fullPath,
   nav: { hidden: true }
